From e935fff1ce6005a7ec75660a0302c527f94710c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:39:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Add the ipaq layout for 240x320 handhelds

The mobintl keys are sized for a phone and its 250 px height is most of a
240x320 screen. The ipaq layout has ten 24 px keys per row and five rows (a
function row with Esc, Tab, Ctl, Alt, arrows and Caps, then three rows of
letters and a bottom row with the layer keys and Space), 100 px high. The
layers are letters (Shift gives the capitals), digits and symbols, and the
Dutch, German and French accents. Rows are relative to the width, so
--dock, --ratio and --corner-radius work unchanged, and so does --width with
--dock, since only a docked layer surface is given a width and the
compositor sizes a full-width one; the man page says so. A layout can now size itself by screen: KBD_DEFAULT_HEIGHT gives
100 px on QVGA portrait, 80 on QVGA landscape, 160 on VGA portrait and 130
on VGA landscape, and -H, -L and the environment still win
(kbd_pick_height). All heights divide by five so no strip stays unused.

The layout has no keymap of its own: keymap.ipaq.h includes the latin keymap
of mobintl, because the Copy keys, the AltGr levels and the COMP key must
stay identical to it, and a copy of 1500 lines would drift. A guard in
keymap.mobintl.h keeps the six other keymaps (about 390 kB of strings) out
of the ipaq binary.

config.ipaq.h turns the popup off, so its surface and its two buffers
(384 kB at 240x100) are never made, and adds DEFAULT_EXCLUSIVE, which
main.c reads like DEFAULT_SHOW_POPUP, so the ipaq keyboard overlaps the
focused app instead of resizing it on every show. --exclusive is the new
inverse of --non-exclusive, -D reports the resolved value, and --help and the
man page mark the default. The font tables are regenerated to include the
euro sign.

kbd_init_layout rounded the accumulated pixel position of each key, and after
floating point error the last key of a row could end one pixel past the
surface (found at --width 200 with this layout). Both key edges are now
rounded from the exact position, so every row ends at the width.

Tests need no compositor. test-ipaq is built with the ipaq layout and keymap
whatever the binary is built for, and checks geometry at 240, 320, 480 and
640 px in both orientations and at docked widths (rows, key sizes, inside
the surface, no overlaps, full rows, at least 20x18 px keys at 240x320), the
height rules, that the bitmap fonts have every label and that the label fits
its key, and that every key gives the keysym of its label through xkbcommon,
including the Copy keys. check-exclusive.sh checks the default and the
options. test-damage made its own pair of layers and its own compose key
when a layout has none.
